+
+### F-309 - Vector stroke and head size were fixed per mark
+
+- Status: resolved
+- Severity: medium
+- Owner: API
+- Observed in: Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/charts/fieldFigures.tsx`, `QuiverView`)
+- Friction: a quiver plot thins the stroke and shortens the head on short
+  vectors, because a full-width stroke and full-size head turn a short arrow
+  into a blob. `vector` took one `strokeWidth` and one `headLength` per mark,
+  so the consumer rounded both values to 0.1 and 0.25 pixel steps, bucketed
+  rows by the rounded pair, and emitted one `vector` mark per bucket with
+  synthetic mark ids. Heads were open chevrons only.
+- Decision: accept `VisualChannel<TDatum, number>` for `strokeWidth` and
+  `headLength`, matching `link` and `stroke`; constants keep working. Add
+  `head: 'open' | 'filled'`, default `'open'`. A filled head is one closed
+  area painted with the stroke color and opacity, and the shaft ends at its
+  base. The filled geometry lives in the vector module, so `arrow` consumers
+  keep byte-identical output.
+- Verification: vector tests cover per-datum stroke widths and head lengths and
+  the filled triangle, shortened shaft, paint, and SVG class. Root TypeScript
+  and the unit suite pass. The isolated arrow static-SVG consumer is
+  byte-identical. The vector consumer grows from 22,218 to 22,341 gzip bytes:
+  2 bytes for the channels and 121 for the filled head, which needs a reviewed
+  vector budget above 21.698 KiB.
