+| `head`          | `'open' \| 'filled'`                 | `'open'`               | Open chevron or closed, filled triangle         |
 
 Length and rotation must be finite. Negative length reverses the body direction
 while preserving the rotation convention. The interaction point remains the
 scaled x/y anchor for every anchor mode.
 
+`strokeWidth` and `headLength` accept a constant or a per-datum accessor, so one
+mark can thin the stroke and shorten the head on short vectors:
+
+```ts
+vector(field, {
+  x: 'x',
+  y: 'y',
+  length: 'magnitude',
+  rotate: 'angle',
+  strokeWidth: (cell) => Math.min(1.5, cell.magnitude / 8),
+  headLength: (cell) => Math.min(5, cell.magnitude / 3),
+  head: 'filled',
+})
+```
+
+A filled head is a closed triangle painted with the stroke color and stroke
+opacity. The shaft stops at the head's base, so a wide stroke does not blunt
+the tip.
+
